    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[css.properties.resize: add support data for replaced elements]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30501</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30501"/>
        <updated>2026-09-13T08:01:07.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264168532?u=430cdb794b33258581ec904970b84130653b6a96&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Add <code class="notranslate">css.properties.resize.replaced_elements</code> and <code class="notranslate">css.properties.resize.iframe</code> subfeatures documenting the CSS UI spec behavior that allows <code class="notranslate">resize</code> on replaced elements and <code class="notranslate">&lt;iframe&gt;</code> regardless of the <code class="notranslate">overflow</code> value.</p>
<p dir="auto">Update <code class="notranslate">css.properties.resize.block_level_support</code> for Firefox: mark as <code class="notranslate">partial_implementation</code> and broaden the note to cover replaced elements (not only <code class="notranslate">&lt;iframe&gt;</code>).</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
